{"id":"n5_u05_l1","unit_id":"n5_u05","instructional_level":"N5","title":"Katakana: dots and circles","goal":"Read voiced and p-sound katakana (ガ ザ ダ バ パ rows) and your first food and object words.","introduces":{"kana":["ka_k_ga","ka_k_gi","ka_k_gu","ka_k_ge","ka_k_go","ka_k_za","ka_k_ji","ka_k_zu","ka_k_ze","ka_k_zo","ka_k_da","ka_k_dji","ka_k_dzu","ka_k_de","ka_k_do","ka_k_ba","ka_k_bi","ka_k_bu","ka_k_be","ka_k_bo","ka_k_pa","ka_k_pi","ka_k_pu","ka_k_pe","ka_k_po"],"vocab":["v_banana","v_pan_k","v_doa","v_piza","v_sarada","v_gasu","v_basu","v_pen","v_terebi","v_piano","v_gorufu","v_dansu"]},"explain":[{"heading":"The same marks as hiragana","body":["Two small dots (゛) voice a katakana as in hiragana: カ → ガ, サ → ザ, タ → ダ, ハ → バ. A small circle (゜) makes the h row into the p row: ハ → パ.","ジ and ヂ sound the same, and ズ and ヅ sound the same. ヂ and ヅ are rare."],"examples":[{"ja":"バナナ","reading":"banana","en":"banana"},{"ja":"ピザ","reading":"piza","en":"pizza"},{"ja":"テレビ","reading":"terebi","en":"television"}]}],"practice":{"question_ids":["q_n5u05_kr01","q_n5u05_kr02","q_n5u05_kr03","q_n5u05_kr04","q_n5u05_kr05","q_n5u05_kr06","q_n5u05_kr07","q_n5u05_kr08","q_n5u05_kr09","q_n5u05_kr10","q_n5u05_kr11","q_n5u05_kr12","q_n5u05_kr13","q_n5u05_kr14","q_n5u05_kr15","q_n5u05_kr16","q_n5u05_kr17","q_n5u05_kr18","q_n5u05_mt01","q_n5u05_mt02","q_n5u05_mt03","q_n5u05_mt04","q_n5u05_rc01","q_n5u05_rc02","q_n5u05_rc03","q_n5u05_rc04","q_n5u05_rc05","q_n5u05_rd01","q_n5u05_rd02","q_n5u05_rd03","q_n5u05_vm_banana","q_n5u05_vm_pan_k","q_n5u05_vm_doa","q_n5u05_vm_piza","q_n5u05_vm_sarada","q_n5u05_vm_gasu","q_n5u05_vm_basu","q_n5u05_vm_pen","q_n5u05_vm_terebi","q_n5u05_vm_piano","q_n5u05_vm_gorufu","q_n5u05_vm_dansu"],"gen":[{"type":"kana_recog","from":"kana","ids":["ka_k_ga","ka_k_gi","ka_k_gu","ka_k_ge","ka_k_go","ka_k_za","ka_k_ji","ka_k_zu","ka_k_ze","ka_k_zo","ka_k_da","ka_k_dji","ka_k_dzu","ka_k_de","ka_k_do","ka_k_ba","ka_k_bi","ka_k_bu","ka_k_be","ka_k_bo","ka_k_pa","ka_k_pi"