{"id":"n5_u05_l2","unit_id":"n5_u05","instructional_level":"N5","title":"Small ッ and the long dash ー","goal":"Read the pause of ッ and the long vowel mark ー in loanwords.","introduces":{"kana":["ka_k_sokuon","ka_k_choon"],"vocab":["v_koohii","v_keeki","v_karee","v_raamen","v_biiru","v_suupu","v_takushii","v_nooto","v_sakkaa","v_suupaa","v_kappu","v_beddo"]},"explain":[{"heading":"ッ is a pause, ー is a long vowel","body":["A small ッ before a consonant makes a short pause and doubles the sound: カップ (kappu), サッカー (sakkaa).","In katakana a long vowel is written with ー: コーヒー (koohii), ケーキ (keeki). The dash always repeats the vowel before it. Each ー is one beat."],"examples":[{"ja":"コーヒー","reading":"koohii","en":"coffee"},{"ja":"ケーキ","reading":"keeki","en":"cake"},{"ja":"カップ","reading":"kappu","en":"cup"}]}],"practice":{"question_ids":["q_n5u05_ch01","q_n5u05_ch02","q_n5u05_ch03","q_n5u05_ch04","q_n5u05_ch05","q_n5u05_ch06","q_n5u05_rd04","q_n5u05_rd05","q_n5u05_rd06","q_n5u05_vm_koohii","q_n5u05_vm_keeki","q_n5u05_vm_karee","q_n5u05_vm_raamen","q_n5u05_vm_biiru","q_n5u05_vm_suupu","q_n5u05_vm_takushii","q_n5u05_vm_nooto","q_n5u05_vm_sakkaa","q_n5u05_vm_suupaa","q_n5u05_vm_kappu","q_n5u05_vm_beddo"]},"exit_check":{"question_ids":["q_n5u05_ch01","q_n5u05_ch02","q_n5u05_ch03","q_n5u05_ch04","q_n5u05_ch05","q_n5u05_ch06","q_n5u05_rd04","q_n5u05_rd06"],"pass":0.7},"provenance":"orig"},
{"id":"n5_u05_l3","unit_id":"n5_u05","instructional_level":"N5","title":"Combined katakana: ャ ュ ョ","goal":"Read combined katakana in food and everyday words.","introduces":{"kana":["ka_k_kya","ka_k_kyu","ka_k_kyo","ka_k_sha","ka_k_shu","ka_k_sho","ka_k_cha","ka_k_chu","ka_k_cho","ka_k_nya","ka_k_nyu","ka_k_nyo","ka_k_hya","ka_k_hyu","ka_k_hyo","ka_k_mya","ka_k_myu","ka_k_myo","ka_k_rya","ka_k_ryu","ka_k_ryo","ka_k_gya","ka_k_gyu","ka_k_gyo","ka_k_ja","ka_k_ju","ka_k_jo","ka_k_bya","ka_k_byu","ka_k_byo","ka_k_pya","ka_k_pyu","ka_k_pyo"],"vocab":["v_juusu","v_chokoreeto","v_shatsu","v_shawaa","v_nyuusu","v_jamu","v_kyabetsu","v_yooguruto","v_chiizu","v_gyooza"]},"explain":[{"heading":"A small kana after an イ-column kana","body":["The same rule as hiragana: キ + ャ = キャ (kya), シ + ュ = シュ (shu), チ + ョ = チョ (cho). The small kana is much smaller than the big one.","ジャ ジュ ジョ read \"ja, ju, jo\"."],"examples":[{"ja":"ジュース","reading":"juusu","en":"juice"},{"ja":"シャツ","reading":"shatsu","en":"shirt"},{"ja":"チョコレート","reading":"chokoreeto","en":"chocolate"}]}],"practice":{"question_ids":["q_n5u05_ky01","q_n5u05_ky02","q_n5u05_ky03","q_n5u05_ky04","q_n5u05_ky05","q_n5u05_ky06","q_n5u05_ky07","q_n5u05_ky08","q_n5u05_ky09","q_n5u05_ky10","q_n5u05_ky11","q_n5u05_ky12","q_n5u05_mt05","q_n5u05_mt06","q_n5u05_mt07","q_n5u05_rc06","q_n5u05_rc07","q_n5u05_rc08","q_n5u05_rc09","q_n5u05_rc10","q_n5u05_rc11","q_n5u05_rc12","q_n5u05_rd07","q_n5u05_rd08","q_n5u05_rd09","q_n5u05_rd10","q_n5u05_vm_juusu","q_n5u05_vm_chokoreeto","q_n5u05_vm_shatsu","q_n5u05_vm_shawaa","q_n5u05_vm_nyuusu","q_n5u05_vm_jamu","q_n5u05_vm_kyabetsu","q_n5u05_vm_yooguruto","q_n5u05_vm_chiizu","q_n5u05_vm_gyooza"],"gen":[{"type":"kana_recog","from":"kana","ids":["ka_k_kya","ka_k_kyu","ka_k_kyo","ka_k_sha","ka_k_shu","ka_k_sho","ka_k_cha","ka_k_chu","ka_k_cho","ka_k_nya","ka_k_nyu","ka_k_nyo","ka_k_hya","ka_k_hyu","ka_k_hyo","ka_k_mya","ka_k_myu","ka_k_myo","ka_k_rya","ka_k_ryu","ka_k_ryo","ka_k_gya","ka_k_gyu","ka_k_gyo"